Who is the most important person in the kingdom?
At that time, the disciples came to Jesus. They asked him, "Who is the most important person in the kingdom of heaven?"
Jesus called a little child to come to Him. He let the child stand among them.
Jesus said, "What I tell you is true. You must change and become like little children. If you don't, you will never enter the Kingdom of Heaven."
Whosoever becomes free from pride like this child is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven.
Anyone who welcomes a little one like this in my name welcomes me.
But what if one of these little ones who believe in me goes astray? If he does, it would be better to tie a large millstone around his neck and throw him into the depths of the sea.
How terrible it will be for the world because of the things that cause people to sin! These things must come. But how terrible it will be for those who cause them!
If your hand or foot causes you to sin, cut it off and throw it away. It is better for you to enter the kingdom of heaven with one hand or one foot than to enter the eternal fire with two hands and two feet. In the eternal fire, the fire burns forever.
If your eye causes you to sin, tear it out and throw it away. It is better for you to enter the kingdom of heaven with one eye than to have two eyes and be thrown into hellfire. The parable of the lost sheep.
