The server fell to his knees in front of him. "Give me time," he asked. "To pay you back everything."
Sido felt it in him. He forgave him for what he owed him and let him go.
The other servant went out and found one of his servants who owed him a little money. He seized him and began to strangle him. He said to him, "Pay me what you owe me!"
The other servant fell on his knees. "Give me time," he asked of him. "To pay you back."
The first servant refused. Instead, he walked away and left the man to be imprisoned. The man would remain in prison until he could repay what he owed.
The other servants saw what happened. He tortured them a lot. They went and told their master everything that happened.
And so, the master called the first slave. He said to him: "O evil slave, I forgive you for everything you owe, because you stained me and asked me for it."
Wouldn't it have been more merciful to spare the other person, just as you showed mercy to me?
In his anger, his master handed him over to the guards. To be punished until he repaid everything he owed.
This is how the Lord will treat in the heavens each one of you, unless you forgive your brother from your heart.
Jesus teaches about divorce.
When Jesus had finished saying these things, he left Galilee and went into the region of Judea on the other side of the Jordan River.
Large crowds followed him. He healed them immediately.
Some Pharisees came to test him. They asked, "Is it lawful for a man to divorce his wife for any and every reason?"
Jesus replied, "Haven't you read that at the beginning the Creator 'made them male and female'? (Genesis 1:27)
He said, 'Therefore a man shall leave his father and his mother, and be joined to his wife; and they shall become one flesh.' (Genesis 2:24)
They are no longer two, but one. Therefore, man cannot separate what God has put together.
They asked, "Why did Moses command that a man give his wife a divorce certificate and send her away?"
Jesus replied, "Moses let you divorce your wives because you were stubborn. But it was not like that from the beginning."
Hani, let me tell you. Anyone who divorces his wife and marries another woman commits adultery. A man can divorce his wife if she is disobedient to him.
