The Workers in the Vineyard.
The Kingdom of Heaven is like a man who had a piece of land. He went out early in the morning to hire workers for his vineyard.
He agreed to pay them the usual wage for a day's work. Then he sent them into his vineyard.
About nine o'clock he went out again. He saw other men standing about in the market and doing nothing.
He told them, 'You too, go and work in my vineyard. I will give you what is right.'
They left. "He went out again around noon and at three o'clock, and did the same thing again."
Around five o'clock, he went out and found others standing around him. He asked them, "Why do you stand here all day and do nothing?"
"Because no one has appointed us," they answered Him. He said to them, "You also go and work in My vineyard."
When the evening came, the owner of the vineyard spoke to the one who was in charge of the workers. He said to him, "Call the workers and give them their pay. Begin with those whom you hired last. And after that, go to those who were before them."
The workers who were hired around five o'clock arrived. Each one received the usual day's wages.
When those who were first appointed came, they expected to receive more. However, each one of them also received the usual day's wage.
